<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8888] Possible data loss during starting of the nodes with empty pds</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8888</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Case:&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1)Start 3 data nodes and activate the cluster with cache with 1 backup and&#160;PartitionLossPolicy.READ_ONLY_SAFE.&lt;br/&gt;
2)Start client and add the data to your cache. Stop the client&lt;br/&gt;
3)Stop DN2 and clear it pds and val&lt;br/&gt;
4)Start DN2. Rebalance will start.&lt;br/&gt;
5)During rebalance stop DN3.&lt;br/&gt;
6)Start DN3.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At this moment some partitions from DN2 marked as LOST and cache size will be less than expected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;7) Run&#160;resetLostPartitions(caches).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now all partitions on DN2 marked as OWNING but cache size is still less than expected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Workaround:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;after step 6 do:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;7)force rebalance using deactivate/activate methods.&lt;br/&gt;
8)wait for completion of rebalance&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now cache size is expected but some partitions from DN2 marked as LOST&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;9)Run&#160;resetLostPartitions(caches).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now cache size is OK and all partitions from DN2 marked as OWNING.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, looks like without force rebalance we have data loss here.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
